    "title": "Boston crowd mocks Philadelphia fans with chant in Celtics Game 1 rout",
    "text": "CelticsBoston Celtics forward Jayson Tatum goes in for a dunk against the Philadelphia 76ers during the first half in Game 1 of a first-round NBA playoffs basketball game, Sunday, April 19, 2026, in Boston. (AP Photo/Robert F. Bukaty)APBy Brian Robb | brobb@masslive.comThe TD Garden crowd enjoyed a dominant Celtics win over the 76ers on Sunday in Game 1 of their first-round series and couldn’t help but have some fun with Sixers fans amid the rout. Philadelphia fans at Xfinity Mobile Arena chanted “We want Boston” in the closing minutes of the Sixers’ win over the Magic Wednesday night in the play-in tournament that sealed a first-round matchup with the Celtics. With the Celtics leading by as many as 35 points in their 123-91 win over the Sixers in Game 1, Boston fans took advantage of the lopsided margin to strike back against Philadelphia fans for the chant. The TD Garden crowd spontaneously chanted, “We want Boston!” on multiple occasions throughout the fourth quarter, openly mocking Sixers fans for wanting to face off with the Eastern Conference title favorites. Joe Mazzulla was asked about the creative chant after the Game 1 win for Boston. “I didn’t really think anything of it,” Mazzulla said. “There is a history to the series which you have to appreciate but at the same time, you have to focus on the task at hand. The most important thing is the stuff we can control. I thought the crowd was great tonight, helped get off to a good start. Playoff basketball. It means more and it’s different in Boston, which we appreciate.” The Celtics and Sixers have faced off in 22 playoff series before this year in what has been a historic NBA rivalry. However, Boston has won the last six series dating back to 1982. That streak looks likely to continue with Joel Embiid sidelined indefinitely, making the Celtics heavy favorites in this series in the 2 vs. 7 matchup. The Celtics host Game 2 at TD Garden against the Sixers on Tuesday night. Experts release early Celtics vs. 76ers Game 3 prediction despite Joel Embiid uncertaintySpurs star Victor Wembanyama in concussion protocol after brutal fall in Game 2Former Celtics big man has huge night in upset Game 2 win over SpursLeBron James gushes about former Celtics guard after Game 2 upset vs. Rockets Brian covers the Celtics and NBA for MassLive.com. He has covered the Celtics since 2010 with previous stops at NBA.com, Bleacher Report and Boston.com. You can reach Brian at BRobb@masslive.com or on Twitter...",
